        "fx_desc_ai_depth_map": "Uses AI to estimate how far each point of the photo or video is and shows it in gray: near is light, far is dark.",
        "fx_desc_blur_gaussian": "Smooth, adjustable blur with a direction — you can blur a single axis.",
        "fx_desc_blur_lens": "Lens blur: a disc of samples shaped like the iris, where bright areas weigh more — this is bokeh, not a smear.",
        "fx_desc_blur_radial": "Spin blur around a center or zoom blur out of it, with adjustable quality.",
        "fx_desc_blur_sharpen": "Brings out detail and edges without inventing texture.",
        "fx_desc_blur_unsharp": "A real unsharp mask: original + gain × (original − blurred), with a threshold so grain is not amplified.",
        "fx_desc_blur_zoom": "Radial streak: the edges travel further than the centre, as when you push the lens. The amount is the fraction of the distance to the centre.",
        "fx_desc_color_balance_hls": "Rotates hue, lightens toward white or darkens toward black and adjusts saturation, all in one control.",
        "fx_desc_color_brightness_contrast": "Raises brightness and opens or closes contrast around mid grey.",
        "fx_desc_color_colorama": "Remaps color: each pixel's brightness becomes a position on a rotating rainbow.",
        "fx_desc_color_curves": "The tone curve: fine control of light and of each color channel.",
        "fx_desc_color_exposure": "Brightens or darkens like camera exposure: multiplies light without blowing out color.",
        "fx_desc_color_fill": "Covers the layer with a flat colour. Opacity is how much the paint covers the image, and whatever was transparent stays transparent.",
        "fx_desc_color_hue_saturation": "Rotates hue, adjusts saturation and lightness, or colorizes everything in a single tone.",
        "fx_desc_color_invert": "The negative: every color becomes its opposite, like a badly developed film.",
        "fx_desc_color_levels": "Sets where black starts, where white ends and where the middle sits.",
        "fx_desc_color_matrix": "Mixes the R, G and B channels together: swaps, adds and crosses colors.",
        "fx_desc_color_saturation": "Makes color more vivid, or takes everything to black and white.",
        "fx_desc_color_tint": "Paints the shadows one color and the highlights another — cinema duotone.",
        "fx_desc_control_angle": "An angle you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_checkbox": "An on/off switch you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_color": "A color you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_point": "An X/Y point you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_slider": "A value from 0 to 100 you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_distort_bulge": "Pushes the middle of the image out, or pulls it in, inside a radius. Outside the radius nothing changes.",
        "fx_desc_distort_displacement_map": "Moves pixels by the values of another layer (the map): pick a channel per axis and the maximum displacement. With no layer, it uses the image itself.",
        "fx_desc_distort_mirror": "Reflects one half of the layer onto the other across a line through the center, at any angle.",
        "fx_desc_distort_ripple_dissolve": "The image vanishes in circles growing from the center with a rippling edge. Animate the progress to turn it into a transition.",
        "fx_desc_distort_shake": "Deterministic shake: the layer shakes the same way every time you reopen the project, with separate frequency and axes.",
        "fx_desc_distort_turbulence": "A noise field pushes every pixel. The field evolves over time — smoke, heat, water.",
        "fx_desc_distort_warp": "Lens: push, pull, twist, sphere and corner, each with its own radius and point.",
        "fx_desc_distort_wave_warp": "A wave crosses the image — horizontal, vertical or diagonal — and can be pinned at the edges.",
        "fx_desc_generate_audio_spectrum": "Draws a layer's audio spectrum as bars, lines or dots along a line or a circle, with adjustable colors and height.",
        "fx_desc_generate_four_color_gradient": "Four points, four colors: a gradient that blends the colors between the points, with softness, noise and opacity.",
        "fx_desc_generate_fractal_noise": "Generates clouds, smoke and textures from fractal noise: noise type, octaves, contrast, scale and animatable evolution.",
        "fx_desc_generate_gradient_ramp": "Linear or radial gradient between two points and two colors, with scatter and a blend with the original.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_cross": "Two bars, one vertical and one horizontal, scan the image reading from the wrong place. Animate the progress to turn it into a transition.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_dissolve_shake": "The layer shakes and breaks into noisy fragments that fly off and fade — animates on its own, no keyframes.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_glitchify": "Digital glitch: the image breaks into sliding blocks, the channels split apart and whole blocks jump out of place.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_signal": "Broadcast signal: lost bands, slipping sync and constant drift.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_uni_vhs": "Stylised VHS: heavy RGB split, wobble, dirty glow and vignette — the vocabulary of tape at the service of the look.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_vhs": "Real VHS: blur, smeared chroma, tracking instability, tape dropouts, scanlines and color degradation.",
        "fx_desc_key_chroma": "Removes the green or blue background and cleans the color spill on the edge.",
        "fx_desc_key_luma": "Removes the black (or the white) from the layer and lets the rest show through.",
        "fx_desc_key_matte_refine": "Chokes or grows a keyed matte and feathers its edge; shows the matte to check it.",
        "fx_desc_light_deep_glow": "Optical glow with a smooth threshold, exposure and multi-scale light falloff.",
        "fx_desc_light_glow": "Spreads the light from the bright parts: the glow that comes off the screen.",
        "fx_desc_light_rays": "Light rays coming from a point: the brightness of the highlights spreads in straight lines.",
        "fx_desc_light_sweep": "A blade of light crosses the image. With relief, it lights only where the surface faces it.",
        "fx_desc_motion_oscillate": "Moves the layer back and forth along a direction, with optional spin and scale pulse; decay lets the motion settle on its own.",
        "fx_desc_motion_swing": "Swings the layer like a pendulum around a pivot, with frequency, phase and decay.",
        "fx_desc_motion_twitch": "Shakes the layer in jolts: each jolt jumps to a new position, rotation and scale, held or eased into the next. Repeatable by seed.",
        "fx_desc_motion_wiggle": "Smooth, repeatable random motion in position, rotation and scale, each channel with its own amount.",
        "fx_desc_omino_diffusion": "Reduce the palette and propagate color errors into directional bands and distortion. More samples cost more GPU time.",
        "fx_desc_oscillate_cycles": "Moves the layer in cycles along an angle, in depth or in orbit. Animated frequency accumulates motion; phase sets the point in the cycle.",
        "fx_desc_pattern_checkerboard": "Alternating cells painted over the layer, with adjustable size, anchor, rotation and edge softness.",
        "fx_desc_pattern_hexagonal": "The honeycomb mesh as cell outlines: a hexagonal LED panel, a glass roof.",
        "fx_desc_shape3d_layout": "Rotates, delays, spreads and randomizes the parts of a 3D shape, like 3D text letters.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_border": "A solid outline around the silhouette of the layer, with colour and width in pixels.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_crt_emulator": "Your image on a tube TV: curved screen, scanlines, RGB phosphor mask, misconverged colors, bloom, flicker and a rolling bar.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_drop_shadow": "The silhouette of the layer, offset, blurred and painted behind it. Separates text and shapes from the background.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_film_damage": "Damaged film: dust, scratches, flicker, gate weave, burns and splices — each with its own control.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_find_edges": "Draws the edges of the image: dark lines on white or glowing edges on black.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_grain": "Film grain: crystal at whatever size you want, luma and chroma apart, stronger in the shadows.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_halftone": "Halftone: the image becomes dots, with the grid rotated per channel so the three screens do not fight.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_holomatrix": "Hologram: the image becomes a projection, with a technical grid, scanlines and interference.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_jpeg_damage": "JPEG damage: the blocks, the ringing on edges and color at half resolution. Quality scales all three.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_minimax": "Dilates or erodes what is bright: thickens or thins a cutout and cleans up a one-pixel edge.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_mosaic": "Turns the layer into single-color cells; with gaps, round cells and shading it becomes an LED panel.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_motion_tile": "Repeats the whole layer as tiles attached to it until they cover the frame. Phase offsets rows (or columns) like bricks, mirror matches the seams and output crops a window at the centre of the frame.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_pixel_sort": "Sorts the pixels of each row by brightness: the image melts into streaks.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_scanlines": "Screen scanlines: the line darkens whatever is behind it, with its own height, softness and channel.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_stroke_outline": "A stroke around the silhouette of any layer (keyed video, PNG, precomp): width, color, softness and position outside, centered or inside.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_vignette": "Darkens (or lightens) the edges of the layer, with adjustable size, softness, shape and color.",
        "fx_desc_time_echo": "Leaves a trail: copies of the image itself delayed in time, with fade.",
        "fx_desc_time_motion_detect": "Shows only what moved: compares the frame with an earlier frame and lights up the differences.",
        "fx_desc_time_posterize": "Locks the frame rate: the image starts moving in steps, like hand-drawn animation.",
        "fx_desc_time_warp_rgb": "Each color channel comes from a different instant: red from the frame behind, blue from the frame ahead.",
        "fx_desc_transform": "Moves, rotates, scales and changes the layer's opacity without losing quality.",
        "fx_desc_transform_crop": "Crops the four edges of the layer by percentage, with an optional soft edge.",
        "fx_desc_transition_box_wipe": "Reveals or hides the layer through a rectangle in its proportions that grows or shrinks from a center.",
        "fx_desc_transition_iris_wipe": "Reveals or hides the layer through a circle or polygon that opens or closes from a center.",
        "fx_desc_transition_venetian_blinds": "Hides the layer in parallel strips that close together, in the direction and number you choose.",
